  "query_preview": "..\nTyphoon Saudel is currently moving over Agrihan, and will pass \nthrough the Mariana chain over the next few hours. However, Invest \n97W northwest of Yap is strengthening. This will prolong and \nintensify the persistent southwest monsoon, with locally heavy \nrainfall developing from Guam northward to Rota over the next 72 \nhours. This will allow the southwest monsoon flow to actually \nstrengthen, especially Sunday through Monday night for Guam and the \nsouth central CNMI. MIMIC water vapor imagery shows the higher \nprecipitable water values moving north across Guam and it's coastal \nwaters, with the previously drier air from Rota to Saipan moistening.\nThis may allow heavier rainfall to develop, even if showers are more\nscattered in coverage tonight and Sunday. With this in mind, the new\nforecast package attempts to convey this, along for increasing \npotential area-wide Sunday night into Tuesday.",
